The optional native `--measure` launch flag instruments visible gameplay
without changing the fixed tick or presentation policy. It times host
loop work through successful submission, samples RSS every 120 drawn
frames, and records one oldest applied local SDL event age per frame.
Only nonempty admitted action batches enter the timing ledger; rejected
batches retain their original timestamp through retry. Execution of
their actual target tick makes them eligible for a subsequent successful
gameplay submission. Remote input, physical scanout and GPU completion
are not measured. Pausing or changing the logical or drawable extent,
viewport or display settings separates reports; skipped submissions do
not create frame samples. The exact submitted presentation layout is
retained by the renderer, avoiding a second drawable query.

