Visible `--measure` sessions additionally report the oldest remote control
age from authenticated host-worker decode completion through its executed
fixed tick and successful gameplay submission. It is separate from the
SDL-clock local input age, excludes lifecycle messages and heartbeats,
and retains the original decode time if fixed-queue admission is delayed.
Both ledgers keep at most one oldest timestamp per admitted tick and
clear applied observations when gameplay is suspended. A segment's first
frame can contribute remote age without a fabricated cadence interval;
subsequent frames use the existing cadence meter's input distribution.
Inline regressions verify independent local and remote ages, absence of
repeated samples, pending-tick retention and suspension. These measures
exclude client-side input, pre-decode network transit and scanout.

